# Ranked by size (S/M/L) then expected payoff within each tier.
# Context: Psychoacoustic model levers (TNS, bmask/SFM-tonality, PNS threshold
# scaling) are exhausted. Codebook DP sectioning (PR #402) and Bit Reservoir control
# are already addressed. Main quality MOS gaps vs Apple AAC & FDK-AAC are:
# 1) LC Core (96k-256k & 56k LC): ~0.15-0.35 MOS gap despite FAAC having top-tier
#    stereo & transient fidelity. Root cause: Scalefactor rate-distortion optimization
#    and joint window-sequence selection.
# 2) HE-v1 Profile (32k-96k HE): ~0.4-0.5 MOS gap (3.51-4.01 vs 3.71-4.49). Root cause:
#    SBR envelope border sharing across channels, SBR noise floor/invf estimation,
#    and SBR noise Huffman encoding.

## Small (isolated bug/tuning, contained blast radius)
- investigate 16k_mono_40k bitrate-targeting outlier (17.0% error vs aac-enc's
  2.1%, worse than Apple's 14.2%) -- low-samplerate/high-relative-bitrate mistargeting
  bug, isolated from stereo quality.
  Levers to try:
  - Audit `CalcBandwidth` sfb cutoff and `quantqual` exponential curve scaling for Fs <= 16 kHz.
  - Check `bitReservoirCap` bounds under 16 kHz mono frame sizes (1024 / 512 samples) to prevent over-allocation.
- HE-AAC v1: Use dedicated noise Huffman tables in write_sbr_noise (saving SBR
  header & payload bits for core LC spectral data).
  Levers to try:
  - Implement 3D/packed SBR noise Huffman table coding in `libfaac/sbr_bitstream.c` using standard ISO/IEC 14496-3 Table 4.63 instead of uncompressed differential bits.
- add PCE (Program Config Element) or 4-bit AudioSpecificConfig support.

## Medium (contained algorithmic change, one subsystem)
- LC Core: Rate-distortion (R-D) scalefactor loop tuning & spectral hole filling
  [leaderboard: FAAC LC at 96k-256k achieves 4.52-4.94 MOS vs Apple's 4.71-4.98 and
  fdkaac's 4.67-4.95 despite identical stereo fidelity (0.97-0.99) and transient timing.
  Iterative distortion-rate scalefactor adjustment (instead of single-pass quantization)
  prevents over-quantization and spectral holes in high-frequency bands]
  Levers to try:
  - Inner/outer loop scalefactor iteration in `libfaac/quantize.c`: Evaluate distortion vs mask ratio (`dist / thr`) per SFB and iteratively increment/decrement `sf[band]` when distortion exceeds SMR threshold.
  - Non-zero spectral hole protection: Prevent single isolated zeroed bands between active harmonic SFBs by capping maximum scalefactor delta (`diff <= 60`).
  - Trellis-based scalar quantization per MDCT line to decide between rounding down (`q`) vs rounding up (`q + 1`) based on exact bit cost vs MDCT reconstruction error.
- HE-AAC v1: SBR noise floor / invf mode derivation from within-band tonality
  [leaderboard: HE-v1 MOS lags by ~0.4-0.5 MOS at 40k-64k stereo. Inaccurate inverse
  filtering (invf) and noise floor estimation cause audible metallic SBR artifacts]
  Levers to try:
  - Derivation of `bs_invf_mode[ch][band]` in `libfaac/sbr.c` using spectral flatness measure (SFM) and pitch autocorrelation on QMF sub-band energy matrices (`sbr_envR`).
  - Adapt SBR noise energy levels (`sbr_noiseR`) dynamically based on transient envelope count (`numEnvelopes`) to prevent noise over-injection during attack transients.
- HE-AAC v1: Move numEnvelopes/eff_amp_res/tEnv to SBRChannel for independent borders
  [current SBR implementation shares envelope time borders across L/R channels;
  independent channel envelope borders prevent temporal smearing on asymmetric transients]
  Levers to try:
  - Refactor `SBRChannel` struct in `libfaac/sbr_internal.h` to hold per-channel `tEnv[]`, `numEnvelopes`, and `sbr_grid`.
  - Update `SbrGrid()` in `libfaac/sbr.c` to detect transients per-channel independently before coupling/decoupling grid borders based on inter-channel transient correlation.

## Large (cross-cutting, higher risk, higher potential payoff)
- Joint CPE block switching & window shape selection
  [currently window shape/sequence selection operates per-channel prior to CPE grouping;
  joint L/R window sequence optimization avoids window shape mismatches between M/S
  channels, which reduces pre-echo and improves coding efficiency across 24k-64k LC/HE stereo]
  Levers to try:
  - Evaluate joint perceptual entropy (`PE_L + PE_R` vs transient thresholds) in `libfaac/blockswitch.c` to force common `window_sequence` (e.g. `EIGHT_SHORT_SEQUENCE`) on CPE pairs whenever either channel contains a transient onset.
  - Synchronize Kaiser-Bessel-Derived (KBD) vs Sine window shape decisions across L and R in CPE elements to optimize M/S coding gain.
- HE-AAC v2 (Parametric Stereo) support for ultra-low bitrates (16k-24k stereo)
  [fdkaac & Apple AAC achieve ~3.28 MOS at 24k stereo using HE-v2 PS, whereas FAAC relies on
  HE-v1 stereo (3.25 MOS) or LC stereo (2.27 MOS)]
  Levers to try:
  - Implement lightweight Parametric Stereo (PS) bitstream syntax (`write_ps_data`) and inter-channel coherence (ICC) / inter-channel phase difference (IPD) estimation in `libfaac/sbr.c` when bitrate per channel <= 8 kbps (16k total stereo).
